# Any local Python virtualenv, wherever it's created (/stress-test finding, 2026-09-02):
# .venv_stress_verify/ (58MB, DuckDB stdlib bindings) was relying SOLELY on its own
# auto-generated internal .gitignore (a `*` rule every `python -m venv` writes) to stay out of
# this PUBLIC repo's history -- nothing at the repo-root level actually covered it. That's fragile:
# any venv tool that doesn't self-ignore, or a `git add -f`, would land 58MB of binaries in public
# git history. Covers this one explicitly, plus any future differently-named venv.
.venv_stress_verify/
.venv/
venv/
